5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Farhood</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Dimassi</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Lehtinen</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Exposure to war-related traumatic events, prevalence of PTSD, and general psychiatric morbidity in a civilian population from Southern Lebanon</article-title><source>J Transcult Nurs</source><year>2006</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>333</fpage><lpage>340</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16946115</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/1043659606291549</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>American Psychiatric Association</collab></person-group><source>Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders</source><year>1994</year><edition>Fourth</edition><publisher-name>Washington DC: American Psychiatric Association</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mollica</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Donelan</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Tor</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The effect of trauma and confinement on functional health and mental health status of Cambodians living in Thailand-Cambodia border camps</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>1993</year><volume>270</volume><fpage>581</fpage><lpage>586</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8331755</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.270.5.581</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Somasudaram</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sivayokan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></